fast-php builds on ideas and code from fast-anything
(https://github.com/EL4CTEO/fast-anything), MIT licensed:

- examples/fuzzy-dedupe-cli/app.php and fuzzy.php are fast-anything's examples/fuzzy-dedupe-php.
- rust/spike-ext/src/fuzzy.rs and examples/fuzzy-dedupe-cli/reference/port.rs follow fast-anything's
  examples/fuzzy-dedupe-php/reference/port.rs.
- src/Analysis/Ranker.php ports the ranking in fast-anything's src/hotspot.rs (outermost portable
  caller, the 2% threshold).
- src/Analysis/Blockers.php starts from the I/O and non-determinism lists in src/php/describe.php.
- res/rec.php's reservoir sampling and derived inputs follow src/php/rec.php.
- src/Port/Task.php follows the structure of task_md in src/native.rs.
- rust/spike-ffi and the Upstream class in spike/crossing.php reproduce fast-anything's PHP bridge
  (src/native.rs glue_rs, src/php/bridge.php) so the two bridges can be measured side by side.

fastphp-std (rust/fastphp-std) re-implements PHP builtins in Rust following their implementation
in php-src (https://github.com/php/php-src): among others _php_math_round and
_php_math_number_format_ex (ext/standard/math.c), zend_gcvt (Zend/zend_strtod.c),
_is_numeric_string_ex, zendi_smart_strcmp and zend_compare (Zend/zend_operators.c),
php_similar_char and php_charmask (ext/standard/string.c), and the match loops of
ext/pcre/php_pcre.c. php-src is licensed under the PHP License v3.01:
This product includes PHP software, freely available from <http://www.php.net/software/>.
